  Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay <tomc@tctechstuff.com> and the ReXGlue contributors.
  BSD 3-Clause License: see LICENSE. ReIGlue is ReXGlue with changes on top; the
  license, copyright notices and history of ReXGlue are kept unchanged.

Xenia
  https://xenia.jp, https://github.com/xenia-project/xenia
  Copyright (c) 2022, Ben Vanik and Xenia project contributors.
  ReXGlue's runtime and Xenos GPU emulation are derived from Xenia (see LICENSE).
  Many ReIGlue changes port later Xenia fixes; their commit messages name them.

xenia-canary
  https://github.com/xenia-canary/xenia-canary
  Copyright (c) 2015, Ben Vanik.
  BSD 3-Clause License (the Xenia terms in LICENSE). PPC instruction tests in
  tests/ppc/asm from its src/xenia/cpu/ppc/testing (commit 48b318a2ad):
  instr_vmaddfp.s, instr_vmaddfp128.s, instr_vmaddcfp128.s, instr_vnmsubfp.s
  and instr_vnmsubfp128.s as they are there, the first three cases of
  instr_vmsum3fp128.s and instr_vmsum4fp128.s, and cases it recorded on an
  Xbox 360, unchanged subsets of its instr__gen_*.s files (the *_hw.s files).

Pinyon Shift
  https://github.com/arcanite24/pinyon-shift
  https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk
  Copyright (c) 2026, Pinyon Shift contributors.
  BSD 3-Clause License: see LICENSE-Pinyon-Shift. Adapted here: the native
  ultrawide presentation and HUD viewport transforms (0063), the scRGB HDR
  presenter, highlight curve and HUD coverage shaders (0091), the contraction
  part of its macOS pixel-math tuning (0082), and the small code model on Linux
  x86-64 (0400). The already-loaded-only RenderDoc probe (0407) follows Pinyon
  Shift's approach; its DynamicLibrary integration and tests are authored here.
  The swap that no longer waits for the frame's replay (0414) follows its
  vulkan_present_on_submission_worker (ShiftGlue 960d853).
  The thread placement by name on Linux (0415) follows its linux_thread_cores
  (ShiftGlue 2849938), rule syntax and Steam Deck layout included.

ShiftGlue
  https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk
  Pinyon Shift's fork of ReXGlue. Its code is under ReXGlue's license, the
  same text as LICENSE here (Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay, with the Xenia
  notice), not under LICENSE-Pinyon-Shift, which covers the Pinyon Shift game
  repository's own files. Adapted here (changes by Brandon G. Neri in
  ShiftGlue): the 0xE0000000 view mapped at its exact offset on Windows, with
  placeholder views (0405).

ShiftGlue
  https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk
  Pinyon Shift's fork of ReXGlue. Its code is under ReXGlue's license, the
  same text as LICENSE here (Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay, with the Xenia
  notice), not under LICENSE-Pinyon-Shift, which covers the Pinyon Shift game
  repository's own files. Adapted here (changes by Brandon G. Neri in
  ShiftGlue): the vector float instructions as the Xbox 360 computes them,
  checked against xenia-canary's cases: a fused vmaddfp and vnmsubfp (0416),
  vmaxfp and vminfp with its NaN, zero and denormal rules (0417), and
  vmsum3fp128 and vmsum4fp128 summed in float64 in vectors (0418).

ReGPU
  https://github.com/zer0ducksgiven/ReGPU, https://github.com/FH1-ReImagined/ReGPU
  Scott's Direct3D 12 Xenos renderer, MIT License. No ReGPU code is included. The
  seam-safe sampling of the car paint's dirt map (0423) follows the idea of its
  Forza Motorsport 2 port (zer0ducksgiven/Forza-Motorsport-2-ReGPU 916b085): the
  vertex shader also outputs frac(u + 0.5), and the pixel shader takes whichever u
  changes less across the pixel.

Downloaded at configure time, not stored in this repository (pinned revisions,
SHA-256 checked; each license is installed beside the GPU library):
  NVIDIA DLSS SDK headers and loader (NVIDIA's license in that SDK), for 0046.
  AMD FidelityFX SDK FSR 3.1 shaders (MIT), for 0072.
  SMAA by Jorge Jimenez et al., iryoku/smaa (MIT), for 0077.

